Focus on behaviour rather than exhaustive automation.

---

# 11. Definition of Done

Sprint 1 is complete when a brand-new user can:

* Install the app
* Create an account
* Browse a trail
* Visit a participating business
* Scan a QR code
* Receive a Passport stamp
* View the stamp in their Passport

without developer intervention.

---

# 12. Out of Scope

Deferred until later sprints:

* Achievements
* Collections
* Notifications
* Community reports
* Offers
* Analytics
* Moderation
* Offline synchronisation
* Leaderboards
* Events

---

# 13. Risks

Primary risks include:

* Scope creep
* Overengineering
* Premature optimisation
* Building administration too early
* Trying to perfect the UI before proving the workflow

---

# 14. Success Measures

Sprint 1 succeeds when:

* Architecture proves sound
* Authentication works
* QR validation works
* Passport updates correctly
* The first complete user journey can be demonstrated

Most importantly:

> A real user earns their first Passport Stamp.

---

# 15. Sprint Retrospective

At the end of the sprint we should ask:

* What worked well?
* What surprised us?
* Which assumptions were wrong?
* What should change before Sprint 2?
* Which areas slowed development?
* Did the documentation reduce uncertainty?

---

# Sprint Principle

> **Build one complete journey before building many incomplete ones.**

